      "text": "### Background on \"Glassy-eyed\" by Ama Owusu\n\n**Author Profile:**\nAma Owusu, born in Kumasi, Ghana in 1990, is a debut novelist who completed her BA in English and Linguistics at the University of Ghana in 2012 and an MFA in Creative Writing at the University of East Anglia in 2015. Her short fiction has been featured in renowned publications such as *Granta*, *Jalada Africa*, and *Transition*. *Glassy-eyed*, published by Cassava Press in 2023, is her first novel, and she is reportedly working on a second novel.\n\n**Critical Reception:**\n*Glassy-eyed* has received significant recognition, being longlisted for the Etisalat Prize for Literature 2023. Early reviews have been positive, with notable mentions including:\n- **The Africa Report:** Four-star rating\n- **Chimurenga:** Highly recommended\n- **Brittle Paper:** Selected as an Editor's Choice\nThe novel has also been nominated for the Literary Blog Award for Best African Fiction Debut 2023 and is shortlisted for the Commonwealth Writers Prize (Africa region) in 2024.\n\n**Content Overview:**\nSet in contemporary Accra, *Glassy-eyed* is a multigenerational literary novel that navigates the lives of three generations of a family through the unique perspective of a glass-blower's workshop. Owusu draws inspiration from her childhood experiences near such a workshop, highlighting the interplay of light and functionality in glass-making as a metaphor for familial relationships and cultural heritage.\n\nFor more detailed insights, you can find additional information and reader opinions on:\n- [Glassy-eyed — Cassava Press](https://openbooks.net/books/glassy-eyed)\n- [Ama Owusu — Author Profile](https://openbooks.net/authors/ama-owusu)\n- [Glassy-eyed — Critical Round-Up](https://openbooks.net/reviews/glassy-eyed)\n\nOverall, *Glassy-eyed* has established Ama Owusu as a promising voice in contemporary African literature, with compelling storytelling that connects personal and cultural narratives.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
